In-game menu (F1) with Graphics, Cheats and Save tabs; graphics settings change while playing.
gow_ajustes_vivo.h (header-only atomics, read once from the launcher's variables) feeds the presentation pass (scaling
filter, sharpness, FXAA, stretch), texture anisotropy and the FPS counter; the menu also sets the window FPS limit and
VSync. F2 still opens the cheats; the ImGui runtime debugger moves to Ctrl+F1 and registers its memory-card copy for the
menu's Save tab. Portuguese menu texts (the menu fell back to English for pt).
Fix: with FXAA on, the presentation shader returned the FXAA colour and skipped the sharp bicubic scaler; FXAA now runs
at the game's resolution into a render target and the scaler maps that onto the window.
TOBIICHI_PANTALLA=sin_bordes opens a borderless window over the monitor (F11 toggles), for capture/scaling tools.
The guest frame function is always wrapped so the counter can be turned on in game (one increment per guest frame).
Tested: game build, in-game screenshots of the menu (pt, 1280x720) and of borderless FXAA+sharp at 1920x1080.

diff --git a/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/gow_ajustes_vivo.h b/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/gow_ajustes_vivo.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/gow_ajustes_vivo.h
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+#pragma once
+// gow-native-pc (patch 39): graphics settings the in-game menu (F1) changes while playing. They start from the
+// launcher's variables and are read where they apply: the presentation pass (main thread), texture sampling (GS
+// thread) and the window. Header-only so the renderer does not link against the menu. Changes last for the session;
+// the launcher stays the place where settings are saved.
+#include <atomic>
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstring>
+#include <string>
+
+namespace gow_vivo
+{
+    inline std::atomic<bool> fxaa{false};
+    inline std::atomic<bool> nitido{true};     // bicubic + adaptive sharpen when magnifying; false = bilinear
+    inline std::atomic<float> nitidez{0.4f};   // GOW_SHARPEN, 0..0.5
+    inline std::atomic<int> aniso{1};          // GOW_ANISO, 1 (off) .. 16
+    inline std::atomic<bool> estirar{false};   // TOBIICHI_ASPECTO=estirar: fill the window, ignore the aspect
+    inline std::atomic<bool> mostrarFps{false}; // TOBIICHI_FPS_GOSTER
+    // Set by the debug panel when it is built in: copies the memory card (F1 > Save). Returns a status line.
+    inline std::atomic<std::string (*)()> copiarSave{nullptr};
+
+    // Reads the launcher's variables once; every reader calls it before its first use.
+    inline void cargar()
+    {
+        static const bool cargado = []
+        {
+            const char *scaler = std::getenv("GOW_SCALER");
+            nitido.store(!(scaler && std::strcmp(scaler, "bilinear") == 0), std::memory_order_relaxed);
+            if (const char *v = std::getenv("GOW_SHARPEN"))
+            {
+                const float s = static_cast<float>(std::atof(v));
+                nitidez.store(s < 0.0f ? 0.0f : (s > 0.5f ? 0.5f : s), std::memory_order_relaxed);
+            }
+            const char *f = std::getenv("TOBIICHI_FXAA");
+            fxaa.store(f && f[0] == '1', std::memory_order_relaxed);
+            if (const char *v = std::getenv("GOW_ANISO"))
+            {
+                const int a = std::atoi(v);
+                aniso.store(a < 1 ? 1 : (a > 16 ? 16 : a), std::memory_order_relaxed);
+            }
+            const char *aspecto = std::getenv("TOBIICHI_ASPECTO");
+            estirar.store(aspecto && std::strcmp(aspecto, "estirar") == 0, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+            const char *fps = std::getenv("TOBIICHI_FPS_GOSTER");
+            mostrarFps.store(fps && fps[0] == '1', std::memory_order_relaxed);
+            return true;
+        }();
+        (void)cargado;
+    }
+}
